     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"With mfa_admin deployed, the attacker can get partway in but cannot reach exfiltration. They can phish the workstation (foothold_workstation, stolen_user), exploit web and proxy, and pivot internally, since segmentation is not deployed. From there they can authenticate to the appserver and kerberoast to get stolen_admin. However, auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin, so foothold_dc is unreachable. auth_dc is the only route to foothold_dc, so admin_dc and dump_dbadmin_dc are also unreachable, and stolen_dbadmin is never obtained. Without stolen_dbadmin, auth_db and auth_fileserver cannot fire. That means no foothold or admin on the db or fileserver, so neither exfiltrate_db nor exfiltrate_fileserver can be used.\"}"
    }
   ],
